===Etymology===
From {{inh|sa|iir-pro|*HáH}}, from {{inh|sa|ine-pro|*h₂éd|t=to, at}}. Cognate with {{cog|gem-pro|*at}} (whence {{cog|en|at}}) and {{cog|la|ad}}. The final ''*d'' in the Proto-Indo-European term regularly alternated with ''*h₁'', the latter appearing before certain consonants originally. Sanskrit generalized the form ending in ''*h₁'' and its fellow Indo-European cognates generalized the form ending in ''*d''.<ref>{{cite-journal|last=Garnier|first=Romain|title=Nouvelles réflexions sur l’effet-Kortlandt|date=2014|journal=Glotta|pages=140-160|publisher=Vandenhoeck & Ruprecht|volume=90|language=French}}</ref>

